      "F6": "The failure to obtain fluid on percutaneous aspiration makes an abscess less likely, but does not rule out a pilonidal cyst or other cystic structure.",
      "F9": "The description of the excised mass as complex and septated is more suggestive of a soft tissue tumor or cystic structure, but the lack of involvement of the coccyx or anal sphincter makes a pilonidal cyst less likely."
